# 03 Exploratory Analysis

This notebook explores patterns in the cleaned dataset, focusing on fit outcomes across demographics, categories, and size tiers.

```python
import pandas as pd
import seaborn as sns
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Load cleaned data
path = '../data/processed/renttherunway_cleaned.csv'
df = pd.read_csv(path)

# Basic stats
print('Total records:', len(df))
print('Fit distribution:')
print(df['fit'].value_counts(normalize=True))

# Non‑fit rate by category (≥200 rows)
cat_counts = df.groupby('category').size()
cat_nonfit = df[df['fit'].isin(['small', 'large'])].groupby('category').size()
cat_rate = (cat_nonfit / cat_counts).fillna(0)
cat_rate = cat_rate[cat_counts >= 200].sort_values(ascending=False)
print('\nTop 10 categories by non‑fit rate:')
print(cat_rate.head(10))

# Plot non‑fit rate by size group
size_rate = df.groupby('size_group').apply(lambda g: (g['fit'].isin(['small','large']).mean()))
size_rate.plot(kind='bar', color='steelblue')
plt.title('Non‑Fit Rate by Size Group')
plt.ylabel('Rate')
plt.show()

# Correlation heatmap for numeric fields
numeric_cols = ['height_cm','weight_kg','age','rating','bmi']
corr = df[numeric_cols].corr()
sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, cmap='coolwarm')
plt.title('Correlation Matrix')
plt.show()
```

The visualizations generated here are saved in `dashboard/charts/` for later inclusion in the Tableau dashboard.
